    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d874">

                <pb facs="1018" n="1006" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg1006"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.60H11/305</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-11">May 11, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador of Yugoslavia called to see me this morning at his request.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador expressed deep appreciation for the opportunity which the
                    President had given him of talking with him last week. He told me that he had
                    urgently submitted, in the name of the King <pb facs="1019" n="1007"
                        xml:id="pg1007"/> of Yugoslavia, the request to the President that American
                    Army officers be detailed as attaches to General Mihailovich at his headquarters
                    in Montenegro. He said that the President had asked whether the Ambassador had
                    discussed this with Lord Halifax<anchor n="49" xml:id="d874-f1"/> and, when Mr.
                    Fotitch had replied that he had not, the President had made a memorandum of the
                    point and had said that he would take the matter up.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d874-f1" n="49" xml:id="d874-f1-content">
                <p>British Ambassador.</p>
            </note>
